		<p>In this article we will see <strong>How to integrate Stripe Api in CodeIgniter 4</strong>, with the use of <strong>Stripe Payment Gateway</strong>, we will create a form with <strong>stripe checkout</strong> and we will do some tests in <strong>test mode</strong>.</p>

		<h2>How to integrate Stripe Api in CodeIgniter 4?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>We will first install the package with <strong>composer</strong>, go to the root of your project and run the following command <code>composer require stripe/stripe-php</code>, which adds the most recent version, check later in the file <strong>composer.json</strong>, where says <strong>require</strong>.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/stripe1.png" alt="stripe1">

		</div>

		<p>We will create the form for the checkout, <strong>PK will be the publishable key</strong>, which we will use only in the views, and we have the <strong>SK secret key that will be for operations with the back-end</strong> and <strong>test because we are in test mode</strong>.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		namespace App\Controllers;


		use Stripe\Stripe;
		use Stripe\Customer;
		use Stripe\Charge;


		class Customers extends BaseController
		{

			public function __construct()
			{		
				$stripe = Stripe::setApiKey('sk_test_yourApiKey');

			}

			public function index()
			{
				return view('customers');
			}

			public function createCustomer()
			{

				$customer = Customer::create([
					'email' => $this->request->getPost('stripeEmail'),
					'source'  => $this->request->getPost('stripeToken'),
					'description' => 'Full access'
				]);

				$charge = Charge::create([
					'customer' => $customer->id,         
					'amount'   => 79900,
					'currency' => 'usd'
				]);

				dd($customer);	

			}
			}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>Adding the checkout in the view, we will only use the <strong>PK</strong>.</p>
